IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `ccc-core`
IMPORT `ccc20-part16-interpretation`

-- ccc20-tests-interpretation.l4 -- tests for ccc20-part16-interpretation.l4 (ss 493, 493.01). Expected values are hand-written from the text of lines 11036-11055.

§ `Tests -- section 493 "accused includes"`

-- (a) a peace officer has issued an appearance notice under s 497; (b) arrested for a criminal offence. "includes": neither is not covered.
#ASSERT `s 493 the person is an accused within the definition` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 493 the person is an accused within the definition` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 493 the person is an accused within the definition` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 493 the person is an accused within the definition` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Tests -- section 493 "judge means"`

-- (a) Ontario: a judge of the superior court of criminal jurisdiction of the Province.
#ASSERT `s 493 the person is a judge as defined in section 493` Ontario `s 493 a judge of the superior court of criminal jurisdiction of the province` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 493 the person is a judge as defined in section 493` Ontario `s 493 a judge of the Supreme Court` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 493 the person is a judge as defined in section 493` Ontario `s 493 three judges of the Court of Quebec` EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- (b) Quebec: a judge of the superior court of criminal jurisdiction of the province, or three judges of the Court of Quebec.
#ASSERT `s 493 the person is a judge as defined in section 493` Quebec `s 493 a judge of the superior court of criminal jurisdiction of the province` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 493 the person is a judge as defined in section 493` Quebec `s 493 three judges of the Court of Quebec` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 493 the person is a judge as defined in section 493` Quebec `s 493 a judge of the Nunavut Court of Justice` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 493 the person is a judge as defined in section 493` Quebec `s 493 an office that is none of those` EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- (d) the eight Provinces named: a judge of the superior court of criminal jurisdiction of the Province (one assertion for each province), and no other office.
#ASSERT `s 493 the person is a judge as defined in section 493` `Nova Scotia` `s 493 a judge of the superior court of criminal jurisdiction of the province` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 493 the person is a judge as defined in section 493` `New Brunswick` `s 493 a judge of the superior court of criminal jurisdiction of the province` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 493 the person is a judge as defined in section 493` Manitoba `s 493 a judge of the superior court of criminal jurisdiction of the province` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 493 the person is a judge as defined in section 493` `British Columbia` `s 493 a judge of the superior court of criminal jurisdiction of the province` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 493 the person is a judge as defined in section 493` `Prince Edward Island` `s 493 a judge of the superior court of criminal jurisdiction of the province` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 493 the person is a judge as defined in section 493` Saskatchewan `s 493 a judge of the superior court of criminal jurisdiction of the province` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 493 the person is a judge as defined in section 493` Alberta `s 493 a judge of the superior court of criminal jurisdiction of the province` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 493 the person is a judge as defined in section 493` `Newfoundland and Labrador` `s 493 a judge of the superior court of criminal jurisdiction of the province` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 493 the person is a judge as defined in section 493` Alberta `s 493 three judges of the Court of Quebec` EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- (e) Yukon and the Northwest Territories: a judge of the Supreme Court.
#ASSERT `s 493 the person is a judge as defined in section 493` Yukon `s 493 a judge of the Supreme Court` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 493 the person is a judge as defined in section 493` `Northwest Territories` `s 493 a judge of the Supreme Court` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 493 the person is a judge as defined in section 493` Yukon `s 493 a judge of the Nunavut Court of Justice` EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- (f) Nunavut: a judge of the Nunavut Court of Justice.
#ASSERT `s 493 the person is a judge as defined in section 493` Nunavut `s 493 a judge of the Nunavut Court of Justice` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 493 the person is a judge as defined in section 493` Nunavut `s 493 a judge of the Supreme Court` EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- the seam of s 2 "release order": BOOLEAN
#ASSERT `s 493 the maker of the order is a judge as defined in section 493` Ontario `s 493 a judge of the superior court of criminal jurisdiction of the province`
#ASSERT NOT (`s 493 the maker of the order is a judge as defined in section 493` Ontario `s 493 a judge of the Supreme Court`)
#ASSERT `s 493 the maker of the order is a judge as defined in section 493` Quebec `s 493 three judges of the Court of Quebec`

-- the helper for paragraphs (a) and (d): a judge of the superior court of criminal jurisdiction of the Province.
#ASSERT `s 493 ordinary province` `s 493 a judge of the superior court of criminal jurisdiction of the province` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 493 ordinary province` `s 493 a judge of the Supreme Court` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 493 ordinary province` `s 493 an office that is none of those` EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- the helper for paragraph (e), Yukon and the Northwest Territories: a judge of the Supreme Court.
#ASSERT `s 493 territory with a Supreme Court` `s 493 a judge of the Supreme Court` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 493 territory with a Supreme Court` `s 493 a judge of the superior court of criminal jurisdiction of the province` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 493 territory with a Supreme Court` `s 493 an office that is none of those` EQUALS JUST FALSE

§ `Tests -- section 493 "warrant"`

-- Form 7 for an arrest warrant, Form 8 for a committal warrant; any other purpose is not covered ("when used in relation to").
#ASSERT `s 493 the document is a warrant within the definition` `s 493 a warrant for the arrest of a person` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 493 the document is a warrant within the definition` `s 493 a warrant for the arrest of a person` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 493 the document is a warrant within the definition` `s 493 a warrant for the committal of a person` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 493 the document is a warrant within the definition` `s 493 a warrant for the committal of a person` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 493 the document is a warrant within the definition` `s 493 a warrant for some other purpose` TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Tests -- section 493.01 "indictable offence"`

-- indictable: yes. Summary only: not also prosecutable by indictment, so no. Both: yes unless the prosecutor elected summary conviction.
#ASSERT `s 493.01 the reference to an indictable offence includes the offence` (`s 493.01 the offence charged` OF `an indictable offence`, FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 493.01 the reference to an indictable offence includes the offence` (`s 493.01 the offence charged` OF `an offence punishable on summary conviction`, FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 493.01 the reference to an indictable offence includes the offence` (`s 493.01 the offence charged` OF `an offence that the section makes both indictable and punishable on summary conviction`, FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 493.01 the reference to an indictable offence includes the offence` (`s 493.01 the offence charged` OF `an offence that the section makes both indictable and punishable on summary conviction`, TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 493.01 the offence is treated as an indictable offence` (`s 493.01 the offence charged` OF `an indictable offence`, FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 493.01 the offence is treated as an indictable offence` (`s 493.01 the offence charged` OF `an offence that the section makes both indictable and punishable on summary conviction`, TRUE))
